<title>SWITZERLAND: Rieter repurchases 178,741 shares.</title>
<headline>Rieter repurchases 178,741 shares.</headline>
<dateline>WINTERTHUR, Switzerland 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss textile machinery and automotive systems maker Rieter Holding said it had repurchased 178,741 registered shares at a price of 440 francs per share.</p>
<p>The share repurchase, together with the price of the offer, was announced on April 8, when Rieter said it would repurchase up to 225,000 shares.</p>
<p>Rieter registered shares were trading at 452.00 francs late on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The repurchase, providing it is approved by shareholders at the company's annual meeting on May 22, would reduce share capital to 47,455,260 Swiss francs from 51,030,080 Swiss francs.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial, +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
